<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Magic and Divine</h1>
<p>Magic (MAG) and divine (DIV) are the two powers behind every spell. Each 
spell draws on one of them:
</p>
<ul><li><b>magic</b>: the spells of sorcerers and conjurers;</li>
<li><b>divine</b>: the spells of healers, druids, paladins, necromancers, dark knights and rangers.</li></ul>
<p>The higher the power a spell draws on, the better you cast it: the more 
a harmful spell hurts, the more a healing spell heals, and the more 
easily you succeed. Your skill in the spell and in its sphere counts as 
well. A target resists your spells with their brain, not their own magic 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Brain</a>), and with their own skill in that spell or its sphere: a 
sorcerer who has mastered fire shrugs off a small fire spell.
</p><p>You raise magic and divine like the other abilities, by training at your 
guild (see <a cmd='#'>Help Abilities</a>). Your race and guild decide how easily they 
grow: a sorcerer's magic, a healer's divine.
</p><p>When your charisma is higher than both your magic and your divine, your 
mana comes back faster; when it is lower, more slowly (see <a cmd='#'>Help 
Charisma</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
